Political Risk Insurance Submission – Sindh Solar Energy Project (SSEP) – Standard Chartered Bank

Dear Team,

We are submitting Standard Chartered Bank PLC (London Branch) for your consideration in respect of Political Risk Insurance for the Sindh Solar Energy Project (SSEP) in Pakistan.

The insured acts as Mandated Lead Arranger and Agent Bank on the USD 410,000,000 senior secured project finance facility for the Sindh Solar Energy Project (SSEP), a 500 MW AC ground-mounted photovoltaic solar power plant.

The insured seeks coverage for Political Risk, specifically Sovereign Non-Payment / Contract Frustration, Currency Inconvertibility, and related sovereign risks arising from the Government of Pakistan and National Transmission & Despatch Company (NTDC).

The policy is proposed for a 15-year term from 1 March 2025 to 28 February 2040, aligned to the facility tenor. The limit of liability is USD 410,000,000, declining in line with the facility amortisation schedule.

